<title>CHINA: Shanghai registers 350 U.S. firms in 1996.</title>
<headline>Shanghai registers 350 U.S. firms in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shanghai registered almost one U.S. company a day last year, with 350 American firms opening offices in the city by the end of 1996, the Business News said on Monday.</p>
<p>A total of 1,991 American-invested firms have registered in Shanghai since 1982, accounting for 12.7 percent of the city's 15,692 foreign-invested firms and contracting $4 billion in investment, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The United States was the largest Western investor in Shanghai in 1995, and the third largest behind Hong Kong and Japan, official figures show.</p>
</text>
